reduce() combines multiple values into one result.
partial() creates specialized versions of existing functions.
lru_cache() improves performance by caching previous results.
cache() provides simple unbounded caching.
wraps() is important when writing decorators.
singledispatch() allows behavior based on the type of the first argument.
Function caching can significantly reduce repeated computation when used appropriately.
